# The changelog is GENERATED by Changesets, and oxfmt formats fenced code blocks inside markdown —
# so a changeset whose `tsx` sample was written with spaces fails `format:check` weeks later, on the
# bot's release PR, over a file no human wrote and nobody reads for indentation. It blocked #250 and
# #255 that way.
#
# oxfmt reads .prettierignore from the directory it runs in, and `format:check` is `oxfmt --check .`
# from here, so this is enough. Nothing else in the package is exempt.
CHANGELOG.md

# Site-image-viewer geometry data, not source. oxfmt would expand these single-line blobs to tens of
# thousands of lines (zone1b-villas.json alone is ~16,900), burying every future diff that touches
# the directory. They are generated/exported data and nobody reads them as code.
src/site-image-viewer/*.json
